  "fire_select": {
   "side": "R",
   "doc": "Firing hand turned on the grip so that its thumb reaches the left selector lever (no reference: inferred). CR-3.  From fire_indexed no thumb pose comes nearer the lever than 10.5 mm, and no small move of the hand nearer than 7.8 mm (checks/selector_reach.json).  This hold is fire_indexed moved as far as the reach needs: a search over the hand's pose and the thumb's joints at three positions of the lever (safe, 58 degrees, fire) for the smallest move with the thumb's glove within reach of the lever at all three, nothing inside the rifle, no finger in the trigger guard, the trigger finger as straight as in fire_indexed, and the arm inside its range for some elbow swivel.  The three other fingers then close on the grip where they can.  The elbow has to come in under the rifle for it (see notes/NOTES.md): this is a hold for the moment of working the lever, not a firing grip.",
